  "topIssues": [
    {
      "id": "I_kwDOOjIlKM76Hwie",
      "title": "postinstall script fails: scripts/install-ollama.js not included in published tarball",
      "author": "edcet",
      "number": 22,
      "repository": "elizaos-plugins/plugin-ollama",
      "body": "## Problem\n\n`bun pm trust --all` fails globally because this package's postinstall script errors:\n\n```\nerror: Module not found \"scripts/install-ollama.js\"\nerror: postinstall script from \"@elizaos/plugin-ollama\" exited with 1\n```\n\nThis blocks `bun pm trust --all` for the entire global install, preventing all other packages from being trusted.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`package.json` declares:\n```json\n\"postinstall\": \"bun scripts/install-ollama.js\"\n```\n\nBut the `files` field is:\n```json\n\"files\": [\"typescript/dist\", \"README.md\", \"python\", \"rust/src\", \"rust/Cargo.toml\"]\n```\n\nThe `scripts/` directory is not in `files`, so it is excluded from the published npm tarball. The file exists in the repo at tag `v1.2.4` (confirmed via GitHub API) but is not shipped to npm.\n\n## Impact\n\nThe postinstall script (`scripts/install-ollama.js`) checks if Ollama is installed and pulls the `nomic-embed-text` model. It is non-critical — the plugin functions without it. The script also skips in CI environments (`CI=true`).\n\nHowever, because `bun pm trust --all` stops at the first error, this blocks trust for all other untrusted packages in the same global install.\n\n## Workaround\n\nSet `CI=true` before running trust:\n```bash\nCI=true bun pm -g trust --all\n```\n\nOr trust packages individually, skipping this one.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd `scripts` to the `files` field:\n```json\n\"files\": [\"typescript/dist\", \"README.md\", \"python\", \"rust/src\", \"rust/Cargo.toml\", \"scripts\"]\n```\n\nNote: there is an existing branch `fix/ollama-install-script-ci` but it does not appear to address this specific issue (its `files` field is `[\"dist\"]` and still declares the postinstall script).\n\n## Environment\n\n- bun 1.3.11\n- @elizaos/plugin-ollama 1.2.4\n- macOS arm64",
      "createdAt": "2026-04-02T18:45:03Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "state": "OPEN",
      "commentCount": 0
    }
  ],
